  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-94833",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, we convert the given probability into a cumulative probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<-1)=0.3783\\,⇒\\,P(X\\le -1)=0.3783\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le -1) & =0.3783 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{-1-2}{\\sigma }) & =0.3783 \\\\ Φ(-\\frac{3}{\\sigma }) & =0.3783 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{\\sigma } & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.3783)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(-0.31)=0.3783\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(0.3783)=-0.31.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sigma } & =-0.31 \\\\ \\sigma  & ≈9.68\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nto $2$ decimal places.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
